# UI test: a borrow that outlives what it points at (SC0333).
#
# Rule 5, checked against the referent's storage-dead points and nothing else
# (§10 item 3). It is the error with nothing to offer but a change of
# signature: there is no lifetime syntax to widen, so the note names the two
# things that do work — return an owned value, or return an index.
#
# It is also where Decision 9 is worth the most, and this file is written to
# make all three of its spans distinct: where the borrow is born (line 3),
# where the referent is declared (line 2), and where the borrow is still needed
# (line 4). Writing `borrowed value` as the tail of the body instead collapses
# the third span onto the whole body — see `tests/ui/README.md`.
#
# The headline is wrong and is pinned wrong on purpose; the README says how.

def escape() -> borrowed Int:
    let value be 5
    let r be borrowed value
    r
